KNOWNBUG libstdcxx16
main.cpp
--cpp26 --object-bits 12 --unwind 8 --no-unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ UTF-8: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
std::text_encoding ([text.encoding]) from a name.  With GCC 16's headers
CBMC failed to parse <utility> in C++26 mode, as cpp26_inplace_vector, and
then the friend operator==(const text_encoding &, id) called itself for
`mib() == __i' (cpp11_builtin_enum_comparison_beats_converting_friend).
Checked with GCC 16.
